/*!
\page page_stTpcPixel StTpcPixel

\brief Single ADC pixel (one pad × one time-bin sample) from the TPC readout.

\ref StTpcPixel represents a single ADC sample at one pad × one time-bin location in the STAR
TPC readout. It is the fundamental unit of raw TPC data below the cluster level. Pixels are
not normally stored persistently during standard reconstruction; they are created transiently by
\ref StTpcRawData::getVecOfPixels "StTpcRawData::getVecOfPixels()" into a caller-supplied
<tt>StVectPixel</tt> vector for embedding diagnostics, cluster visualisation, and hit-finding
studies.

\section sec_pixel_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\verbatim
TObject
└── StObject
    └── StTpcPixel       (concrete — this class)
\endverbatim

\c StTpcPixel objects are produced by \ref StTpcRawData::getVecOfPixels into a
<tt>std::vector<StTpcPixel></tt> and owned by value in that vector.

\section sec_pixel_members Data Members

- <tt>UChar_t mDetector</tt> — Detector identifier (\c StDetectorId cast to byte). For standard
  TPC: \c kTpcId (1); for iTPC sectors: \c kiTpcId (39).
- <tt>UChar_t mSector</tt> — TPC sector number 1–24. Sectors 1–12 are East; 13–24 are West.
- <tt>UChar_t mRow</tt> — Padrow number within the sector (standard TPC: up to 90 rows; iTPC:
  up to 72 rows).
- <tt>UChar_t mPad</tt> — Pad number within the padrow (1-based).
- <tt>UShort_t mTimeBin</tt> — Time-bin index within the TPC drift window (0–511 corresponding
  to ~100 ns per bin, ~51.2 µs total window).
- <tt>UShort_t mAdc</tt> — Raw 10-bit ADC value (0–1023) after 8→10 bit expansion. Zero
  indicates no signal above the zero-suppression threshold.
- <tt>Int_t mIdTruth</tt> — <em>Simulation only.</em> Geant track ID of the primary energy
  deposit. Zero for real data.
- <tt>Short_t mId</tt> — Cluster identifier assigned by the cluster finder; zero if not yet
  assigned.

\section sec_pixel_methods Key Methods

- <tt>unsigned char detector() const</tt> — Returns detector ID byte.
- <tt>unsigned char sector() const</tt> — Sector number (1–24).
- <tt>unsigned char padrow() const</tt> — Padrow number.
- <tt>unsigned char pad() const</tt> — Pad number within the padrow.
- <tt>unsigned short timebin() const</tt> — Time-bin index (0–511).
- <tt>unsigned short adc() const</tt> — Raw ADC value (0–1023).
- <tt>int idTruth() const</tt> — MC truth Geant track ID.
- <tt>short id() const</tt> — Cluster assignment ID.
- <tt>virtual void Print(Option_t*) const</tt> — Prints pixel information to stdout.

\section sec_pixel_ownership Object Ownership

\c StTpcPixel is a plain value type with no heap-allocated members. Pixels from
\ref StTpcRawData::getVecOfPixels are stored by value in a <tt>std::vector<StTpcPixel></tt>
and destroyed when the vector goes out of scope. No special deletion is needed.

\section sec_pixel_usage Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StTpcRawData* rawData = event->tpcRawData();
if (!rawData) return;

StVectPixel pixels;
rawData->getVecOfPixels(pixels, 5 /*sector*/, 20 /*row*/);

for (const StTpcPixel& px : pixels) {
    std::cout << "sec=" << (int)px.sector()
              << " row=" << (int)px.padrow()
              << " pad=" << (int)px.pad()
              << " tb="  << px.timebin()
              << " adc=" << px.adc() << "\n";
}
\endcode

\sa \ref page_stTpcRawData, \ref page_stTpcHit
*/
